1. Objective

    Implemented GitHub commit integration with the Odoo 19 Employee Analytics Dashboard to retrieve employee-wise GitHub contribution details for 2026 and make those details available directly from the employee analytics view.

2. Work Completed

    GitHub webhook integration: Configured the GitHub webhook endpoint to receive push events and store newly pushed commit information in Odoo immediately. This removes the need to wait for a scheduled cron job for new push events.

    2026 commit synchronization: Configured synchronization to retrieve commits from January 1, 2026 onward, with a configurable start date and date-based filtering.

    Employee-wise commit statistics: Added GitHub commit count data to the Employee Analytics Dashboard. The count is based on the same 2026 start-date configuration used by the GitHub integration.

    Time-period filtering: Added support for commit-count views by day, week, month, quarter, year, all-time, and custom date range.

    Employee dashboard card: Added a GitHub commit card to each employee tile. It displays the commit count for the selected period.

    Commit drill-down: Configured the employee commit card so that selecting it opens the corresponding employee's commits in the GitHub module.

3. Synchronization Flow

    An employee pushes commits to the configured GitHub repository.

    GitHub sends a push event to the Odoo webhook endpoint.

    Odoo receives and processes the webhook payload and stores the new commit records.

    Employee mapping associates the commit author with the corresponding Odoo employee, where a valid mapping is configured.

    The Employee Analytics Dashboard displays the employee-wise commit count for the selected date range.

    The one-time historical backfill can be run manually through “Sync GitHub Now” in Settings.

4. QA Testing and Status

    The task was moved through the project workflow and marked Done on November 3, 2026. A QA testing update was recorded on November 2, 2026, stating that complete GitHub integration functionality was under testing on the Employee Management QA server.

    The task activity also records the implementation updates listed above, including webhook-based push handling, 2026 date filtering, employee-wise counts, and the dashboard commit card.

5. Expected Result

    New GitHub push events are received through the webhook and reflected in Odoo without waiting for a scheduled synchronization.

    Commit counts are shown per employee and respond to the selected reporting period.

    Managers can open an employee's commit list from the dashboard card for further review.

    Historical commits from the configured 2026 start date can be retrieved through a manual backfill.